(The same shape with a fixed-size buffer: the buffer is held in one place.)
a number called gate is 1.
If gate is 1 then,
  open a file called cupboard for reading at "/dev/null",
  Close cupboard.
a buffer called cupboard is 65 bytes in size.

To 'fill the cupboard'.
    append "plates" to cupboard.

'fill the cupboard'.
Print "size {cupboard's size}, capacity {cupboard's capacity}".
